{
  "id": "COMPOUND:35682 - PROTEIN:6256",
  "verbalization": "The compound (2R,3R,4S,5S,6R)-2-[[(1R,2R,4R)-2,4-dihydroxy-1,2,3,4-tetrahydronaphthalen-1-yl]oxy]-6-(hydroxymethyl)oxane-3,4,5-triol is associated with Histone H1.0 through multiple pathways. It is identified as a target of Phosphodiesterase 6C, which is itself targeted by several compounds, including 3-(5-Hydroxy-2,3,8,8-Tetramethyl-4-Oxo-3,4-Dihydro-2H,8H-Pyrano[2,3-F]Chromen-6-Yl)-3-Phenyl-Acrylic Acid and 1R,11S-Dihydroxy-8R,13R-Epoxylabd-14-Ene. These compounds, in turn, have Histone H1.0 as their target. Additionally, the compound is also linked to Cetyl octanoate, which also targets Histone H1.0. The evidence suggests that the compound may influence Histone H1.0 through the activation or inhibition of enzymes involved in histone modification, potentially altering chromatin structure and function. The strength of the evidence is consistent across multiple pathways, but the exact mechanism by which the compound interacts with Histone H1.0 remains to be fully elucidated.",
